1
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,640
- Shoot me then. Come on!
- Don't.

2
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:30,920
I'll be able to have you arrested.

3
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,720
- You're taking Fon with us?
- To confirm where we were tonight.

4
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,920
- Where are we going?
- Khon Kaen.

5
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,120
If he comes back, tell him to come see me.

6
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,480
So Liang's not joining us.

7
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,480
If we can't get him on our side,

8
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,640
taking Peng down won't be easy.

9
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:47,720
That guy we met said
there's a boxing match at the fair, right?

10
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:49,520
It's risky there.

11
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,400
The place will be packed.
We don't know who's around. Let's not go.

12
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:54,800
You're a boxer. There's a ring.
You have to fight.

13
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:56,160
Fon, wanna go do something?

14
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,960
- Got it!
- Wow!

15
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,120
You always get one.

16
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:02,720
You already know who's gonna win, right?

17
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,520
It's basically like fixing a fight.

18
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:05,840
Hey, they won't let you fight?

19
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,880
Are you sure it's him?

20
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:11,480
Koh said he saw Oab in Khon Kaen.

21
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,320
He's probably looking for witnesses
to prove they weren't the shooters.

22
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,080
But this time,
I'm the one hunting them down.

23
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,080
- Hey, Dom.
- Up next, a special match.

24
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,640
- You're definitely gonna win. Trust me.
- Just for this event.

25
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:24,760
Not on the schedule. No weight limit.

26
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:27,400
- Last time you lost.
- The odds are one to one.

27
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,640
This time you have to win.

28
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:30,360
- Bet any amount, and you'll get double.
- Knock him out.

29
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,880
Put your guard up, Dom!

30
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:51,440
What the hell?

31
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:57,960
Time!

32
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:06,120
You're completely off today.

33
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,040
Can you even keep fighting?

34
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,280
Put your guard up.

35
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:11,840
Move back if you have to.
Don't just let him hit you.

36
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,120
Hey, why are you smiling?

37
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,400
Are you a sadist?
Your mouth is already full of blood.

38
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:19,840
Fight!

39
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:38,680
- Yeah!
- Get him!

40
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,080
Guard up!

41
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:51,480
You're in top form.

42
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:57,560
- Hey, get it together!
- Keep your guard up.

43
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:59,080
- Come on, man.
- You were letting him hit you.

44
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,480
- One.
- Hey, get up!

45
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,080
Woo!

46
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,320
Come on, wake up!

47
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,720
Get up!

48
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,160
Geez.

49
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,840
That was a good fight.

50
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:38,440
Let's go.

51
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,640
Boss, I won 2,000.

52
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,520
Here.

53
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:52,240
You said your guy was good.

54
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:55,000
How was I supposed to know
his guy would fight this well?

55
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:58,400
One, two, three, four.
I should get at least half of it.

56
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,840
- Thanks a lot.
- Yeah, thanks.

57
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,640
No, I want the cash,

58
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,640
not your hand.

59
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,800
I know. Here.

60
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,840
- Thanks a lot, Dom.
- Yeah.

61
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:10,200
I'll get going.
Next time you come back, let me know.

62
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,560
I'll let you know if something comes up.

63
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,080
- Yeah.
- See you.

64
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,000
See you.

65
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,920
I love the smell of money.

66
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,280
Now we can go home.

67
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,200
Yes.

68
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:32,440
I'm giving all of this to you.

69
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,600
Thank you.

70
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:40,800
One day, I'll get you on a big stage.

71
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,240
That money should've been mine.

72
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:48,200
I arranged the fight and got nothing.

73
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,400
Now I'm losing money because of you.

74
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,040
Hey.

75
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,480
You should've bet on my fighter.

76
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,320
You chose to bet on some random guy.

77
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:38,080
Stop!

78
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:40,560
Take this!

79
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,480
If you want my money, do better.

80
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:40,000
Come here, Oab. Let me help clean you up.

81
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:57,760
Dom, before we go home,
let's stop by the market.

82
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:00,320
What are you buying?

83
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,440
Some medicine.

84
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,320
Sorry to bother you.

85
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,400
Come on in.

86
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,560
Thanks.

87
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:24,680
Here. Your shirt is covered in blood.

88
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:29,280
One is for tonight,
and the other is for tomorrow.

89
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:30,680
Thank you.

90
00:08:35,799 --> 00:08:37,039
Here, Dom.

91
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,680
Does it hurt?

92
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,120
It hurts like hell.

93
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:22,000
You've taken worse hits in fights
and never complained.

94
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:26,920
I don't know. It just hurts more today.

95
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:32,200
How could I forget?
I asked you to be my girlfriend here.

96
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:49,280
You still remember
what size shirt he wears?

97
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:54,440
I just guessed.

98
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,360
I could tell from his build.

99
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:58,560
Really?

100
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:02,600
The last time I saw him was in Grade 12.

101
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:05,080
Even if I did remember,

102
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:07,560
he probably doesn't wear
the same size anymore.

103
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,680
The only size I remember

104
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,520
is yours.

105
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:26,480
Size 44.

106
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:46,280
Go take a shower, Dom.
I'll clean up Oab's wounds.

107
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:53,480
The shirt fits perfectly.

108
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:59,200
You're still the same size
as you were in Grade 12.

109
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:02,080
Let me treat your wounds.

110
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:22,080
<i>The shirt fits perfectly.</i>

111
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,920
<i>You're still the same size</i>

112
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,600
<i>as you were in Grade 12.</i>

113
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:38,960
Don't overthink it.

114
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:56,320
If the police arrest Boss Peng…

115
00:11:58,680 --> 00:11:59,640
will you stop?

116
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:08,440
I'm angry too that Arm never got justice.

117
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:13,160
Ever since I heard about it from you,
I've been looking into the case.

118
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,760
What did you find?

119
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,720
I found out the case was never closed

120
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,120
because they couldn't find the shooter.

121
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:23,480
The investigating officer's name
was also redacted in the documents.

122
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,560
It looks like they stopped investigating.

123
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,280
Exactly.

124
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:31,640
So how can you expect me
to just sit back and do nothing?

125
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:33,520
But I found another case

126
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,120
that might be connected.

127
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,520
What case?

128
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:41,200
Two people were murdered near the border.

129
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:45,640
What's strange is their records
only show murder charges.

130
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:48,680
There's nothing
linking them to drugs at all.

131
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:54,560
They intended to silence them.

132
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:03,440
I'll keep looking into this

133
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:07,080
if you promise to stop

134
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:11,880
and walk away
from this world of influence.

135
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:26,840
I promise.

136
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:47,320
I'll go take a shower first.

137
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,760
My house has two bedrooms.

138
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,560
You and Dom can take one.

139
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:53,360
I'll just sleep here.

140
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:57,920
Dom and I will sleep in the living room.

141
00:13:58,720 --> 00:13:59,680
You go get some rest.

142
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,880
Suit yourself.

143
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:05,840
The pillows and blankets are in the room.

144
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:08,280
You two can get them yourselves.

145
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:22,440
You sleep on the sofa. I'll sleep here.

146
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:25,240
Why bother setting this up?
You didn't have to.

147
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:28,840
Thanks.

148
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:38,560
Do you always keep your gun next to you?

149
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:45,000
You have to stay alert
in this line of work.

150
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,160
You could die any minute.

151
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:34,520
Oab.

152
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,280
Why do you like Fon?

153
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:41,520
Why do you want to know?

154
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:48,520
I mean, she's a police officer.

155
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,400
It just doesn't seem…

156
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,000
Like we don't belong together?

157
00:15:56,720 --> 00:16:00,320
You have money and power.
You could have any woman you want.

158
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,280
So why her?

159
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,120
She's a police officer.

160
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:27,120
Fon and I used to be together.

161
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,080
And we never actually broke up.

162
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,840
I guess it was my fault.

163
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,880
I never contacted her again.

164
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,640
She might think we're over, but…

165
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,360
To me,

166
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:54,680
it never ended.

167
00:16:58,080 --> 00:17:00,280
She's my first love,

168
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:05,200
and she'll always be the only one for me.

169
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:11,960
Get some sleep.

170
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,280
You're driving tomorrow.

171
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:18,600
Hey!

172
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,440
Whoa!

173
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:36,280
- Oab!
- Get back inside.

174
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:37,400
Get back in the room!

175
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,440
Take this!

176
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,240
Watch out!

177
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:08,000
Hey, get back!

178
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,080
Come here.

179
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,680
Come out.

180
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:29,080
You're gonna die anyway.

181
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:34,680
Stay here.

182
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:48,280
Hey!

183
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:21,360
I'm out of bullets.

184
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,080
I have two.

185
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:26,040
There are three of them.

186
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:32,560
You!

187
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:38,360
Shit.

188
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,800
Ma'am!

189
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:45,000
- What is it?
- Can I use your phone?

190
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,160
Why?

191
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,040
Let's go to Fon's room.

192
00:20:50,760 --> 00:20:52,280
Go ahead. I'll cover you.

193
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:55,920
You go. I'll watch your back. Don't worry.

194
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:57,520
I won't let them shoot you.

195
00:20:58,600 --> 00:20:59,840
Go!

196
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:08,000
Follow them!

197
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:09,000
Go!

198
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:11,880
Where's Fon?

199
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:13,680
Damn.

200
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:18,240
What are you doing?

201
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,200
Are you okay?

202
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:59,120
Keep your head down!

203
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:11,640
Hey, don't drag this out.

204
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:13,400
The cops will be here soon. Come on.

205
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:15,480
Hey!

206
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,400
- Dom.
- Dom.

207
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:39,560
Dom.

208
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:41,480
Are you okay?

209
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:43,680
Who sent you?

210
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:47,400
I asked who sent you.

211
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:49,320
Your father.

212
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,960
This is why I disappeared, Fon.

213
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:04,240
I didn't want you caught up in this.

214
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:05,320
EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT

215
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,400
Then who were they?

216
00:23:12,680 --> 00:23:14,560
They were probably sent to take us out.

217
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,920
Was it the promoter from last night?

218
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:21,760
I'm not sure.

219
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,760
But would he really hire four hitmen?

220
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:27,360
That's not cheap.

221
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:43,840
How are you feeling?

222
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:45,080
I'm better now.

223
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:50,560
How did you know
about the guns in the closet?

224
00:23:59,440 --> 00:24:02,360
I found them while cleaning the room.

225
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:32,280
Damn it!

226
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:36,120
I sent four of my men
and they all got killed.

227
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:38,360
This is damn embarrassing

228
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:39,840
Sorry, Boss.

229
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:42,360
If people find out
my hitmen are this useless,

230
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:43,680
who's gonna hire me?

231
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:45,560
Huh?

232
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:49,280
What are you waiting for? Get out!

233
00:24:49,360 --> 00:24:50,680
Just get out of my face!

234
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:51,840
- Yes, Sir.
- Yes.

235
00:24:51,920 --> 00:24:53,360
- Let's go.
- Come on, hurry.

236
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:03,960
Hello?

237
00:25:08,280 --> 00:25:09,480
Is that you, Peng?

238
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:12,360
It hurts, Bro.

239
00:25:12,440 --> 00:25:13,560
Be gentle.

240
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:15,280
I know. I told you to go to the hospital.

241
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:17,360
You wouldn't go, not even for cute nurses.

242
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:19,760
It's only a small wound. I'd look stupid.

243
00:25:22,280 --> 00:25:24,200
I'm so pissed.

244
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:26,400
We pay them all that money,

245
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:27,960
but who are they protecting?

246
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:30,760
Instead of dealing with the problem,

247
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:32,760
they came after me.

248
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:36,760
I'll get it.

249
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:41,040
I told you,
they have a lot of connections.

250
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:43,240
We don't know who's backing them.

251
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:46,400
Some people stay in the shadows.
Some show themselves.

252
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:48,360
Even the people we rely on

253
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:50,400
have to watch their backs.

254
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:54,960
Who's calling, Haw?

255
00:25:55,040 --> 00:25:56,240
It's Oab.

256
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:57,880
Why didn't you call me?

257
00:25:57,960 --> 00:26:00,920
He just called to say
he might not be back today.

258
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,440
He's not coming back today?

259
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:03,840
What's he staying there for?

260
00:26:04,520 --> 00:26:06,080
And what about that female cop?

261
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:07,400
Doesn't she have work?

262
00:26:08,720 --> 00:26:09,600
I don't know, Bro.

263
00:26:10,400 --> 00:26:12,040
If you don't know, why didn't you ask him?

264
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:14,920
Whoa, Oab would say I was being nosy.

265
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:17,320
Are you insulting me?

266
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:19,960
- Wait! Hold on!
- Hey!

267
00:26:20,040 --> 00:26:21,480
Calm down. Both of you, take it easy.

268
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:24,760
- Look at him.
- Yeah, I know. Calm down.

269
00:26:24,840 --> 00:26:27,800
Did you tell Oab
about the box we got yesterday?

270
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:29,760
I did.

271
00:26:29,840 --> 00:26:31,840
I also told him
that Pong had been taken and beaten up

272
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:34,400
and that the chief wanted to see him.

273
00:26:35,120 --> 00:26:37,760
Good. At least you said something useful.

274
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:40,360
And what did he say?

275
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:41,800
He said he'd hurry back.

276
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:46,360
Why didn't you tell me that
from the start, you idiot?

277
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:49,440
How was I supposed to say anything
when you kept yelling at me?

278
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:34,200
How's he doing?

279
00:27:36,400 --> 00:27:38,520
Since we got here, he hasn't said a word.

280
00:27:44,280 --> 00:27:46,160
Fon, go get something to eat.

281
00:27:46,720 --> 00:27:48,280
I'll try talking to Dom.

282
00:28:10,360 --> 00:28:11,600
Hey.

283
00:28:22,720 --> 00:28:24,120
Don't overthink it.

284
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:28,640
If you don't take them out,
they'll take you out.

285
00:28:44,160 --> 00:28:46,200
I used to be like you.

286
00:28:48,320 --> 00:28:50,120
I never thought about killing anyone.

287
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:54,600
I wouldn't even kill an ant.

288
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:01,760
But life taught me that…

289
00:29:04,600 --> 00:29:06,120
if I don't do it first,

290
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:09,160
they'll do it to me.

291
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:29,840
But I think I'm going to quit.

292
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:37,320
Quit?

293
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:42,400
Why?

294
00:29:45,920 --> 00:29:47,240
What happened this morning…

295
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:53,400
made me realize
I'm putting Fon's life at risk.

296
00:29:55,920 --> 00:29:57,360
I can lose everything else,

297
00:29:59,200 --> 00:30:01,240
but I can't lose her.

298
00:30:12,800 --> 00:30:15,040
If I have to leave everything behind

299
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:19,920
so Fon and I can live safely together,

300
00:30:20,840 --> 00:30:21,960
I will.

301
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:50,960
Where are you going?

302
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:53,880
Bangkok.

303
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:57,200
I have something urgent to handle,
so we're leaving early.

304
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,240
Are you okay to go?

305
00:31:01,960 --> 00:31:02,960
I'm fine.

306
00:31:04,800 --> 00:31:07,040
How can Dom drive in this condition?

307
00:31:08,120 --> 00:31:09,280
I'll drive.

308
00:31:10,360 --> 00:31:11,920
If we leave now,
we should get there tonight.

309
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:13,480
Let's go.

310
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:50,520
Call me if you need anything.

311
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:52,440
Okay.

312
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:55,120
Don't forget to take Dom to the hospital.

313
00:31:59,800 --> 00:32:00,720
Fon.

314
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:46,080
If you ever feel
that this still belongs to me

315
00:32:50,120 --> 00:32:51,800
give it back to me then.

316
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:04,320
Like you said before,

317
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:08,680
you might not be the same person
I knew back then. I understand.

318
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:13,000
I may have walked out of your life before

319
00:33:13,560 --> 00:33:15,080
for my own reasons.

320
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:19,520
But this time,

321
00:33:23,080 --> 00:33:24,600
I'm going to win you over again.

322
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:30,360
I'll do whatever it takes
to make you feel the same about me again.

323
00:33:37,520 --> 00:33:38,720
I swear…

324
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:43,520
I'll never leave you again.

325
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:19,080
Stay here for now.

326
00:34:44,400 --> 00:34:45,239
Hey.

327
00:34:45,840 --> 00:34:47,080
When are they getting here?

328
00:34:47,159 --> 00:34:48,239
It's been about nine hours.

329
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:49,719
They should be here by now.

330
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:50,760
They'll be here soon.

331
00:34:52,920 --> 00:34:54,120
They're here.

332
00:35:00,280 --> 00:35:01,600
Why did you drive yourself?

333
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:03,360
Dom got shot.

334
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:06,560
- They came after you there?
- Yeah.

335
00:35:07,160 --> 00:35:08,040
Why didn't you tell us?

336
00:35:08,120 --> 00:35:09,640
- You got shot?
- Yeah.

337
00:35:11,680 --> 00:35:12,720
Who shot you?

338
00:35:12,800 --> 00:35:13,800
I don't know.

339
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:15,520
But they were professionals.

340
00:35:16,040 --> 00:35:16,880
Really?

341
00:35:16,960 --> 00:35:19,520
- Yes.
- Good thing Oab wasn't hurt.

342
00:35:19,600 --> 00:35:20,800
They broke in and shot us.

343
00:35:21,400 --> 00:35:23,200
You're lucky you made it out alive.

344
00:35:25,680 --> 00:35:27,160
So what happened?

345
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:29,120
Why did Oab have to rush back?

346
00:35:49,240 --> 00:35:50,520
If he doesn't agree, we're stuck.

347
00:35:55,600 --> 00:35:57,200
Did you meet Liang?

348
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,520
Yeah.

349
00:35:59,120 --> 00:36:02,640
But if you can't accept his offer,
you're stuck anyway.

350
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,800
Are you going to meet the chief now?

351
00:36:23,360 --> 00:36:25,480
You're still going to pay him?

352
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:34,320
Money solves problems.

353
00:36:37,960 --> 00:36:39,160
Sorry for wasting your time.

354
00:36:39,760 --> 00:36:41,800
Yeah, thanks.

355
00:36:47,880 --> 00:36:50,440
Can't you guys
just keep things under control?

356
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:51,960
I don't want any trouble.

357
00:36:53,280 --> 00:36:55,800
Tell me straight. Was it you

358
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:57,600
who ambushed Peng?

359
00:36:58,640 --> 00:37:00,120
Pong said you had no idea.

360
00:37:01,520 --> 00:37:02,800
He started it.

361
00:37:05,080 --> 00:37:07,080
And he did it in our territory.

362
00:37:10,040 --> 00:37:11,480
Here's the thing.

363
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:14,440
If Peng starts taking over our territory,

364
00:37:15,040 --> 00:37:18,400
my businesses will suffer.
Less business means less income.

365
00:37:18,480 --> 00:37:20,200
Like the bar being closed,

366
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:22,720
there's even less money coming in.
You understand, right?

367
00:37:24,520 --> 00:37:26,040
And besides, I don't want you

368
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:29,760
coming after my people.

369
00:37:34,640 --> 00:37:36,440
Sometimes things get out of hand.

370
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:44,160
I've known you
since your construction days.

371
00:37:44,760 --> 00:37:46,960
I've helped you
get to where you are today.

372
00:37:47,040 --> 00:37:49,680
At this point,
we have to look out for each other.

373
00:37:49,760 --> 00:37:51,960
I help you, you help me.

374
00:37:52,960 --> 00:37:54,480
Don't make things difficult for me.

375
00:37:54,560 --> 00:37:56,600
Because if I get transferred,

376
00:37:57,120 --> 00:37:59,520
you have no idea who the next guy will be,

377
00:37:59,600 --> 00:38:00,960
where he comes from or who he works for.

378
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:02,800
You'll have to start over with him,

379
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:04,680
and that'll make things harder for you.

380
00:38:08,120 --> 00:38:11,000
Alright. I'll make sure my guys behave
so there won't be any problems.

381
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:20,040
And about the bar,

382
00:38:21,280 --> 00:38:23,600
get it cleaned up and ready to reopen.

383
00:38:24,480 --> 00:38:26,280
Your people should've handled it.

384
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:34,720
POLICE REPORT

385
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:47,760
Kiat had to die because of me.

386
00:38:51,240 --> 00:38:53,120
Isn't this just how our lives work?

387
00:38:54,160 --> 00:38:56,680
When you help someone,
you're willing to make sacrifices too.

388
00:39:00,120 --> 00:39:01,360
But still,

389
00:39:01,440 --> 00:39:03,000
you shouldn't have been so nice to him.

390
00:39:03,080 --> 00:39:04,440
He's clearly taking advantage of us.

391
00:39:06,440 --> 00:39:08,800
How would it be any different
if I put a gun to his head?

392
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:10,320
But he threatened us.

393
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:11,560
He's taking our money too.

394
00:39:12,760 --> 00:39:14,440
Isn't he working for us?

395
00:39:17,240 --> 00:39:18,560
He takes our money,

396
00:39:19,840 --> 00:39:21,720
makes the shooting case
against Peng disappear,

397
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:25,920
turns a blind eye,
pretends not to see what we're doing.

398
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:31,080
Having to listen to him complain for a bit
isn't a big deal.

399
00:40:06,440 --> 00:40:07,960
You must be lonely being here alone.

400
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:11,600
Just wait a little bit.

401
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:14,640
I'll bring you a friend.

402
00:40:19,120 --> 00:40:21,600
How is Pong going to win Liang over?

403
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:23,200
I think it'll be difficult.

404
00:40:23,760 --> 00:40:25,280
Exactly.

405
00:40:25,800 --> 00:40:27,240
After everything that just happened,

406
00:40:27,320 --> 00:40:29,040
I think Peng will be even more careful.

407
00:40:29,120 --> 00:40:30,320
Yeah.

408
00:40:33,240 --> 00:40:35,040
So how are we going to get close to him?

409
00:40:36,120 --> 00:40:37,720
We have to become his customer.

410
00:40:39,280 --> 00:40:40,400
For what?

411
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:43,000
Drugs.

412
00:41:00,440 --> 00:41:01,480
Dom?

413
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:03,680
Hello?

414
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:05,760
<i>You're not asleep yet?</i>

415
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:11,200
I was just about to go to sleep.

416
00:41:11,840 --> 00:41:13,040
Did you need something?

417
00:41:13,120 --> 00:41:15,440
I just called to say good night.

418
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:17,920
That's all?

419
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:21,520
Good night.

420
00:41:23,240 --> 00:41:24,320
Okay.

421
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:04,240
Where's Dom?

422
00:42:04,320 --> 00:42:05,440
Oh, hey!

423
00:42:05,520 --> 00:42:06,920
No idea. He left early this morning.

424
00:42:07,880 --> 00:42:09,120
What do you need him for?

425
00:42:10,600 --> 00:42:12,720
Nothing.
I just wanted to ask him something.

426
00:42:21,080 --> 00:42:22,120
Hey, Dom.

427
00:42:22,760 --> 00:42:25,160
Perfect timing. Someone wants to see you.

428
00:42:26,840 --> 00:42:28,160
Where have you been?

429
00:42:29,440 --> 00:42:30,480
I went to the clinic.

430
00:42:34,200 --> 00:42:36,440
I took a shower
and water got into my wound,

431
00:42:36,520 --> 00:42:37,720
so I had to get it treated.

432
00:42:52,240 --> 00:42:53,160
Yes?

433
00:43:21,280 --> 00:43:24,200
I got this from the guys
who attacked us that day.

434
00:43:28,120 --> 00:43:29,720
You're from Khon Kaen, right?

435
00:43:30,960 --> 00:43:33,360
Do you have any friends
you can ask about it?

436
00:43:33,440 --> 00:43:35,640
I'm not sure
if anyone would know anything.

437
00:43:39,480 --> 00:43:41,120
Maybe try asking Fon's father?

438
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:48,080
You want me to call her parents?

439
00:43:48,160 --> 00:43:50,760
Yeah. Her father
is a police officer there, isn't he?

440
00:43:52,040 --> 00:43:54,520
He might have seen
something like this before.

441
00:43:56,080 --> 00:43:57,000
Yes.

442
00:43:57,080 --> 00:43:58,760
But don't tell Fon about this.

443
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:02,840
Got it.

444
00:44:09,720 --> 00:44:11,960
- Hey, Dom.
- Yes, Oab?

445
00:44:12,960 --> 00:44:14,520
I have to go to the den this evening.

446
00:44:15,600 --> 00:44:16,760
Can you take Fon home for me?

447
00:44:18,120 --> 00:44:20,720
I'm worried those guys from Khon Kaen
won't let this go.

448
00:44:22,560 --> 00:44:23,480
Sure.

449
00:44:23,560 --> 00:44:27,240
Oh, and stop by
to buy a small fish tank for her too.

450
00:44:30,400 --> 00:44:31,320
Yes.

451
00:44:51,960 --> 00:44:53,000
Hey.

452
00:44:53,600 --> 00:44:56,800
He shut the door to talk to you.
Was it something serious?

453
00:44:57,400 --> 00:44:58,160
No.

454
00:44:59,960 --> 00:45:01,000
Hey.

455
00:45:01,520 --> 00:45:03,040
What's going on with Liang?

456
00:45:05,120 --> 00:45:06,840
You managed to meet
with him before, right?

457
00:45:08,680 --> 00:45:09,880
Can you still meet with him?

458
00:45:12,840 --> 00:45:14,280
You couldn't close the deal?

459
00:45:14,920 --> 00:45:16,640
He couldn't accept our offer.

460
00:45:17,960 --> 00:45:19,400
What the hell does he want?

461
00:45:24,080 --> 00:45:27,120
POL. MAJ. GEN. SAENCHAI SAENSUWAN

462
00:45:30,560 --> 00:45:31,960
You took forever yesterday.

463
00:45:32,040 --> 00:45:33,640
Were you waiting for me to die first?

464
00:45:35,320 --> 00:45:37,840
If I could've gone in myself,
I would've helped you.

465
00:45:38,360 --> 00:45:40,320
And the local officers
didn't know anything.

466
00:45:42,120 --> 00:45:43,800
Do you know who broke in?

467
00:45:48,560 --> 00:45:50,240
Was it Peng's guys?

468
00:45:50,320 --> 00:45:52,160
Why do you suspect him?

469
00:45:52,880 --> 00:45:54,120
Did Oab tell you?

470
00:45:54,840 --> 00:45:55,800
No.

471
00:45:58,080 --> 00:45:59,600
So why did you go to Khon Kaen?

472
00:46:00,120 --> 00:46:02,000
He wanted to visit my parents.

473
00:46:06,240 --> 00:46:07,480
Really.

474
00:46:10,840 --> 00:46:12,200
Not to set up an alibi, right?

475
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:15,240
An alibi for what?

476
00:46:16,680 --> 00:46:18,120
To make it look like he was in Khon Kaen,

477
00:46:18,960 --> 00:46:21,800
not the one who ambushed Peng
and made him file a report.

478
00:46:30,400 --> 00:46:34,360
He filed a report the same night
you guys went to Khon Kaen.

479
00:46:34,960 --> 00:46:36,360
I just found out from the chief.

480
00:46:39,280 --> 00:46:40,560
Really?

481
00:46:40,640 --> 00:46:44,160
But when we were there,
he really did want to visit my parents.

482
00:46:52,960 --> 00:46:55,240
AMON SOMPHAKUL

483
00:46:56,000 --> 00:46:57,520
Still looking into these cases?

484
00:47:02,720 --> 00:47:04,960
How're you doing?
Is Uncle Toem feeling better?

485
00:47:05,040 --> 00:47:07,440
He's better now. Thank you so much.

486
00:47:09,240 --> 00:47:11,440
- Hello, Auntie.
- Hello.

487
00:47:15,880 --> 00:47:17,000
Hey, Uncle.

488
00:47:24,440 --> 00:47:25,520
Is it crowded?

489
00:47:25,600 --> 00:47:26,640
Yes.

490
00:47:30,360 --> 00:47:33,960
Dum, send some guys
to clean up the bar tomorrow.

491
00:47:34,040 --> 00:47:34,880
Already cleared?

492
00:47:34,960 --> 00:47:37,520
Yeah. We've got a couple of days

493
00:47:37,600 --> 00:47:39,440
to clean up and rearrange the place.

494
00:47:39,520 --> 00:47:40,760
Yeah, okay.

495
00:48:00,760 --> 00:48:01,760
Oab.

496
00:48:12,320 --> 00:48:13,960
Why does he come here every day?

497
00:48:17,120 --> 00:48:18,240
Fon.

498
00:48:20,400 --> 00:48:21,440
Hey.

499
00:48:22,200 --> 00:48:23,360
Did you come with Oab?

500
00:48:24,920 --> 00:48:25,880
No.

501
00:48:26,520 --> 00:48:28,240
Why? Do you want to see him?

502
00:48:29,360 --> 00:48:32,680
I don't. That's why I came out this way.

503
00:48:34,680 --> 00:48:35,920
He asked me to pick you up.

504
00:48:36,000 --> 00:48:39,280
I got here early,
so I went to buy some food for you.

505
00:49:02,560 --> 00:49:04,240
Everything you bought looks so good.

506
00:49:51,080 --> 00:49:51,920
Fon.

507
00:49:53,680 --> 00:49:55,800
When Oab treats you well,

508
00:49:55,880 --> 00:49:56,960
do you ever feel good about it?

509
00:50:01,520 --> 00:50:02,640
What am I supposed to feel?

510
00:50:07,320 --> 00:50:08,600
Are you starting to like him again?

511
00:50:10,120 --> 00:50:11,120
No.

512
00:50:29,080 --> 00:50:31,800
I'm sorry
if I made you feel uncomfortable.

513
00:50:41,640 --> 00:50:42,720
You didn't.

514
00:50:43,600 --> 00:50:44,840
Whatever it is, just ask me.

515
00:50:46,160 --> 00:50:49,760
It's better than keeping it to yourself
until it starts bothering you.

516
00:50:49,840 --> 00:50:53,280
If you ask me, I get the chance to answer

517
00:50:53,920 --> 00:50:57,360
and explain what's really going on.

518
00:51:02,680 --> 00:51:05,120
I'm sorry I didn't trust you,
but Oab is a good guy.

519
00:51:08,520 --> 00:51:10,880
He's so good that I'm scared

520
00:51:10,960 --> 00:51:13,120
you'll fall in love
with him again one day.

521
00:51:19,400 --> 00:51:21,480
I don't want to see him.

522
00:51:23,520 --> 00:51:25,560
I don't want to hold his hand.

523
00:51:31,880 --> 00:51:33,720
And I don't want to hug him.

524
00:51:35,840 --> 00:51:38,080
I'm just doing my job.

525
00:51:38,160 --> 00:51:39,840
You know that, don't you?

526
00:51:51,960 --> 00:51:53,880
I'll end this as soon as possible.

527
00:52:09,280 --> 00:52:10,480
You're selling pretty well.

528
00:52:11,080 --> 00:52:13,440
Not even a week and you're back for more.

529
00:52:13,520 --> 00:52:14,640
Yes, Boss.

530
00:52:18,440 --> 00:52:21,280
You got a little something extra
for me today?

531
00:52:22,440 --> 00:52:23,800
Of course.

532
00:52:24,960 --> 00:52:26,840
Just a little something for you.

533
00:52:30,440 --> 00:52:32,480
If you know anyone who wants to sell,

534
00:52:33,120 --> 00:52:34,560
I'll give you a cut.

535
00:52:36,400 --> 00:52:37,240
Thank you.

536
00:52:38,720 --> 00:52:39,640
Hey.

537
00:52:41,760 --> 00:52:43,280
Where do you sell?

538
00:52:43,800 --> 00:52:45,960
You ran out in less than a week.

539
00:52:47,840 --> 00:52:48,680
Around the gambling den.

540
00:52:48,760 --> 00:52:50,080
Which one?

541
00:52:51,040 --> 00:52:52,240
Phetchaburi.

542
00:52:53,720 --> 00:52:54,800
Better get going.

543
00:52:57,640 --> 00:52:59,560
That's Oab's territory.

544
00:53:08,720 --> 00:53:10,320
Where the hell is the gambling den?

545
00:53:43,360 --> 00:53:44,800
Hey, do you know him?

546
00:53:45,400 --> 00:53:46,680
No idea.

547
00:53:47,280 --> 00:53:48,120
Hey.

548
00:53:49,720 --> 00:53:50,800
Shit.

549
00:53:51,560 --> 00:53:52,880
Hey, wait.

550
00:53:59,800 --> 00:54:01,160
Why are you following me?

551
00:54:04,720 --> 00:54:06,240
What is going on?

552
00:54:08,320 --> 00:54:09,920
- What the hell?
- You sell drugs, right?

553
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:12,440
- I'd be screwed if I told you.
- Screwed?

554
00:54:13,080 --> 00:54:15,080
Hey, let me go!

555
00:54:17,400 --> 00:54:18,440
Here.

556
00:54:20,280 --> 00:54:21,360
Are you a cop?

557
00:54:24,880 --> 00:54:25,720
No.

558
00:54:26,840 --> 00:54:27,920
Damn it.

559
00:54:30,800 --> 00:54:31,840
Give it here.

560
00:54:33,680 --> 00:54:35,240
I thought you were a cop.

561
00:54:35,840 --> 00:54:36,960
I wouldn't have run if I knew.

562
00:54:38,800 --> 00:54:40,280
Why did you chase me anyway?

563
00:54:42,720 --> 00:54:43,960
I want to buy drugs.

564
00:54:51,720 --> 00:54:53,040
I want more drugs.

565
00:54:54,520 --> 00:54:55,880
You want more than that?

566
00:55:00,560 --> 00:55:02,320
With a clean face like yours?

567
00:55:03,560 --> 00:55:05,200
You use that much?

568
00:55:07,640 --> 00:55:09,440
I want to sell.

569
00:55:13,920 --> 00:55:15,240
Why don't you just buy from me?

570
00:55:17,760 --> 00:55:19,440
But you get it from someone else, right?

571
00:55:22,280 --> 00:55:25,080
Yeah. You really know your stuff.

572
00:55:26,520 --> 00:55:28,120
How about this? This time,

573
00:55:28,200 --> 00:55:30,600
I'll buy whatever you have.

574
00:55:31,520 --> 00:55:34,560
But you have to take me
to the person you get it from. Deal?

575
00:55:47,920 --> 00:55:48,960
What do you want?

576
00:55:49,040 --> 00:55:49,960
Uh…

577
00:55:50,840 --> 00:55:52,440
I need more stuff, Boss.

578
00:55:52,520 --> 00:55:55,000
More? You just got some this afternoon.

579
00:55:56,200 --> 00:55:57,720
I already sold it all.

580
00:55:58,320 --> 00:56:00,120
How did it run out that fast?

581
00:56:00,200 --> 00:56:01,640
You weren't set up, were you?

582
00:56:01,720 --> 00:56:02,640
No, Boss.

583
00:56:02,720 --> 00:56:04,360
Did anyone follow you here?

584
00:56:05,680 --> 00:56:06,880
No.

585
00:56:08,440 --> 00:56:09,560
I didn't see anyone.

586
00:56:10,560 --> 00:56:11,520
You can go.

587
00:56:16,600 --> 00:56:17,640
You're selling well.

588
00:56:20,280 --> 00:56:21,160
How much do you want this time?

589
00:56:22,440 --> 00:56:23,640
Same as before.

590
00:56:23,720 --> 00:56:27,000
But I've got a new seller. You interested?

591
00:56:33,360 --> 00:56:36,960
He said he doesn't want anyone
to know he sells drugs.

592
00:56:37,040 --> 00:56:38,920
So he wants to meet privately.

593
00:56:40,240 --> 00:56:41,440
No one comes around here.

594
00:56:46,280 --> 00:56:47,200
Is he buying a lot?

595
00:56:47,280 --> 00:56:48,320
Whoa.

596
00:56:48,400 --> 00:56:49,760
He's taking everything I have.

597
00:57:01,320 --> 00:57:03,080
I'll wait here, Boss.

598
00:57:36,320 --> 00:57:39,280
Did you ask Fon's father
about that matchbox yet?

599
00:57:39,360 --> 00:57:41,600
It's a matchbox
from Boss Koh's hotel in Khon Kaen.

600
00:57:42,600 --> 00:57:44,120
Boss Koh is an influential figure.

601
00:57:44,920 --> 00:57:46,160
He even has a hitman network.

602
00:57:46,240 --> 00:57:48,440
They need to know
that if they don't kill me,

603
00:57:48,520 --> 00:57:49,760
they'll die.

604
00:57:50,360 --> 00:57:52,120
Chat, calm down.

605
00:57:52,640 --> 00:57:53,560
Get out.

606
00:57:57,120 --> 00:57:57,880
Hey!

607
00:58:03,160 --> 00:58:04,320
You bastard!

608
00:58:13,920 --> 00:58:14,720
Honey, are you okay?

609
00:58:14,800 --> 00:58:17,000
I heard people talking at the market.

610
00:58:17,080 --> 00:58:18,240
Are you hurt?

611
00:58:18,320 --> 00:58:20,240
He helped me, so I'm okay.

612
00:58:20,960 --> 00:58:23,600
Dom, this is Liang, my husband.

613
00:58:53,120 --> 00:58:55,320
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
